---
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { MIN_RATING_SOURCES, FACET_MIN_CASINOS } from '../lib/schemas';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title={`About ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`What ${SITE.name} is, who runs it, and the rules it holds itself to when publishing numbers about gambling operators.`}
>
  <h1 class="text-[32px] sm:text-[38px]">About {SITE.name}</h1>

  <Prose>
    <p class="mt-5">
      {SITE.name} answers one question: what do the established casino review platforms
      collectively think of a given crypto casino? Rather than adding a tenth opinion to a
      crowded market, it gathers the opinions that already exist, puts them on one scale, and
      shows the workings.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
      Each casino page lists the rating published by every platform we could find it on, the
      date we checked, and a link to that exact page. The headline score is the plain mean of
      those figures — see <a href="/methodology/">how we rate</a> for the full formula and its
      weaknesses. A casino found on fewer than {MIN_RATING_SOURCES} platforms carries no score at all.
    </p>

    <h2>Rules we hold ourselves to</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        No invented figures. If a rating, bonus amount or licence number could not be verified,
        it is left out and the omission is visible rather than filled with a plausible guess.
      </li>
      <li>
        No paid placement. Position follows the arithmetic. Commission is disclosed on
        <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">its own page</a> and changes nothing about the order.
      </li>
      <li>
        Real drawbacks. Every casino page carries genuine criticism drawn from player
        complaints and bonus terms, not manufactured balance.
      </li>
      <li>
        Lists earn their place. A feature page stays out of search results until it holds at
        least {FACET_MIN_CASINOS} casinos, because a list of two is not a comparison.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who runs it</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is a small independent project, not a media group and not part of any casino
      operator. It has no licence and takes no bets — it is a comparison site, and the only
      thing it sells is a referral.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and contact</h2>
    <p>
      If a number here is wrong, or a casino's terms have changed since we checked, write to
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Corrections take priority over
      everything else on the roadmap.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
